From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:04:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the camera sensor interface
 and ISP

The A733 has a camera sensor interface controller, the CSIC, and an
image signal processor, the ISP, in the video input system. Add their
nodes, disabled.

The windows are the 1 MiB of the CSI and the 4 MiB of the ISP the
manual maps (chapter 2), and their masters are masters 1 and 2 of the
first IOMMU (manual chapter 10). The interrupts are the CSI_* sources
of CPUX, 139 to 140 and 149 to 167, GIC SPI number minus 32 (manual
section 12.2.3.1). Both nodes hold the PD_VI power domain and the bus
reset of CSI_BGR_REG; the ISP has none of its own, and the reset of
the video input system itself is de-asserted by default (manual
section 4.1.6.247).

Each node holds every gate on its register and DMA path as a named
clock: the bus gate, the module clock, the MBUS clock enable of the
CSI or the ISP, and the two gates of the video input system, VID_IN of
AHB_MAT_CLK_GATING_REG bit 2 and of MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING_REG bit 24
(manual sections 4.1.6.245, 4.1.6.244, 4.1.6.246, 4.1.6.84, 4.1.6.82
and 4.1.6.83). The last two are on at reset and clk_disable_unused()
closes them when no node holds them.

They stay disabled until a driver binds them: an enabled node that no
driver binds keeps the PCK-600 from ever calling its sync_state(),
since fw_devlink waits for the consumer, so no power domain that nobody
holds would be switched off.

Not covered: the parent and rate of the module clocks, the sensor ports
and the MIPI and MCLK pins, and a driver. No camera is attached to the
board, and the manual describes no register of the ISP.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the nodes enabled for a test, the clocks
and the reset of both blocks follow runtime PM, PD_VI is on while they
are resumed, the CSIC registers read their reset values, and the ISP
window reads zero (the manual lists no ISP register).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 46 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 75c150ed9a85..7087c4d4e69e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1518,6 +1518,52 @@ dp_out: port@1 {
 			};
 		};
 
+		csic: csic@5800000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-csic";
+			reg = <0x05800000 0x100000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 117 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 118 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 119 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 120 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 107 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 108 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 121 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 122 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 123 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 124 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 125 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 126 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 127 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 133 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 134 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 135 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_CSI>, <&ccu CLK_AHB_VID_IN>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VID_IN>, <&ccu CLK_MBUS_CSI>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_CSI>;
+			clock-names = "bus", "ahb", "mbus", "mclk", "mod";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_CSI>;
+			power-domains = <&pck600 PD_VI>;
+			iommus = <&iommu0 1>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		isp: isp@5900000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-isp";
+			reg = <0x05900000 0x400000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 129 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 130 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 131 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 132 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_CSI>, <&ccu CLK_AHB_VID_IN>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VID_IN>, <&ccu CLK_MBUS_ISP>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_ISP>;
+			clock-names = "bus", "ahb", "mbus", "mclk", "mod";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_CSI>;
+			power-domains = <&pck600 PD_VI>;
+			iommus = <&iommu0 2>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		pcie: pcie@6000000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pcie";
 			reg = <0x06000000 0x400000>,
